1. StripPunct deletes every ASCII punctuation byte (the 32 chars: !"#$%&'()*+,-./:;<=>?@[\\]^_`{|}~)
2. Collapse turns each run of whitespace into a single space
3. Lower ASCII-lowercases
4. Trimmed at the ends always

The existing implementation does: `strings.Join(strings.Fields(strings.ToLower(s)), " ")` which does lower, then fields+join (collapse + trim).

